# Build context for the `web` image (docker-compose.yml sets `build: ./web`, so the
# context is this directory, NOT the repo root - the root .dockerignore does not apply
# here and everything below has to be listed again).
#
# The Dockerfile's build stage does `COPY . .` after installing dependencies from the
# manifests, so anything left in the context is copied into the image layer and, worse,
# is uploaded to the daemon on every build. On the shared host that matters twice over:
# the context travels through /var/lib/docker on a 38 G disk that three neighbouring
# PostgreSQL instances live on, and a stale `.next` copied over the freshly installed
# one is how a build silently ships yesterday's bundle.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- install output
# `npm ci` runs inside the deps stage from package.json + package-lock.json alone.
# A node_modules built on the developer's machine is both the largest thing in this
# directory and the wrong platform's binaries; copying it over the deps stage's own
# tree is exactly the bug this file exists to prevent.
node_modules

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build output
# `npm run build` regenerates these inside the image. A local .next also contains
# absolute host paths and, in dev, a webpack cache of several hundred megabytes.
.next
out
build
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- caches
.cache
.turbo
.swc
.eslintcache
.npm
.yarn
coverage
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
# Nothing in this image reads .env at build time - the containers get their
# environment from the compose `env_file` at RUN time - so a .env here could only
# ever be an accident, and an accident baked into a layer is one `docker save` away
# from being public. `.env.example` is documentation and carries no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- repository / editor
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
